{"kind":"report","text":"Confirmed as S2 enabling scope. Bring forward from S6 only the optional captured expected-revision input, and name it at, as the MVP plan does, so S6 adds nothing but its own views. Rules: omitted at keeps today's behaviour, expectedOf on a fresh summary. Present, at must name exactly the subjects expectedOf would name for that act, with the revisions the card displayed; a missing, extra or malformed subject is refused before anything is signed, with a named reason, and no fresh revision is ever substituted for a captured one. The signed intent's expected is the captured set, and the custody record keeps it, so a re-report shows what was signed. The scope's own revision check is what refuses a stale act; the service adds no second judgment. Card data and the context line carry the displayed revision to the view and the model; the model-visible tool text does not change. Witness as you state: the subject changes between the card read and the act; the captured input refuses, a fresh one accepts, the context line and the signed expected agree, and a duplicate or re-report never re-signs. S6's change, diff and merge and J1's custody expansion stay outside. No existing mechanism satisfies the witness today: #perform at service.ts:438 always computes expected from the fresh summary.","body":{"decision":"confirmed: bring forward from S6 only the optional captured expected-revision input, named at, in the model and app act paths; omitted keeps today's expectedOf; present it must cover exactly the subjects expectedOf would cover or the service refuses before signing; never substitute fresh revisions; the S2 witness is as you state","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c5a9acd02b76015d21d611fdac94b91f154d1f9e","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}